From: axon7m bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] android: NV12 only in widths where minigbm and the soft ISP agree on the stride

minigbm's msm backend aligns NV12 lines to 128 bytes (Venus); libcamera's
software ISP writes NV12 with the width aligned to 8 and has no way to take
the gralloc buffer's stride. Offer only widths that are multiples of 128
(640, 1280, 1920, 2048, ...), so preview and video buffers are not skewed.
---
--- a/src/android/camera_capabilities.cpp
+++ b/src/android/camera_capabilities.cpp
@@ -444,6 +444,14 @@
 	StreamConfiguration &cfg = cameraConfig->at(0);
 
 	for (const Size &res : resolutions) {
+		/*
+		 * axon7m: minigbm aligns NV12 lines to 128 bytes (Venus), and the
+		 * software ISP writes with its own stride (width aligned to 8):
+		 * offer only widths for which both agree.
+		 */
+		if (pixelFormat == formats::NV12 && res.width % 128)
+			continue;
+
 		cfg.pixelFormat = pixelFormat;
 		cfg.size = res;
 
